Z||000000||MooCow||02-04-2001||11:15 AM||||Hey I was wondering how you painted your roof black?  Did you scuff up the sunroof?  I would like to paint my 87 GT with a black roof, but am unsure how to make the paint stick to the glass.<P>                                 Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||02-04-2001||12:36 PM||||Dude!  He didn't paint the sunroof.  I wouldn't recommend scuffing up your glass and painting it.<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||fropuff||02-04-2001||12:56 PM||||Yep, he didn't paint the sunroof.  It just appears that he did because it was so SHINEY!  I also wouldn't suggest painting glass; kind of defeats the purpose of the sunroof.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||02-04-2001||07:10 PM||||If you really want the job done right, have a professional body shop paint it.  Do all the sanding yourself though, if you can, that way you'll save a lot of $$ on labor.  They'll do a good job taping off everything, so your sunroof will have no harm done to it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||02-04-2001||09:15 PM||||O I thought he painted the sunroof.  What kind of paint did he use then to make it look like glass almost?  I already have all the body panels off cause I am doing the sides, then putting it back together and taping it all off.  It is only gonna cost me $100 to get it painted.  All I had to do was the labor and buy the paint.<P>                             Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||02-04-2001||11:06 PM||||The best thing would be to remove the sunroof altogether when you paint the roof.  You'll get good paint around the edges.<P>Just make sure you mask and use good paper when you paint.  I'd cut a piece of cardboard to fit in the opening and mask around it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||02-05-2001||08:10 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst_pearl.jpg">   <P>heh.. NOPE didn't shoot the glass... i took the sunroof out threw away the old seal and removed the entire roof panel. hit it with 400grit sand paper then cleaned it with an RM made Prep Sol. it's a wax and grease remover. then shot it with a mixing black. (most of the blacks you see have other colors mixed in i had access to the mixing room so just used the straight black mixing pigment. It's Sikkens Epoxy Based coating. if you thinking of doing it yourself a PPG or Dupont DBU or Deltron 2000. are easy to work with and cost effective. Laquor is ok but it's a LOT of work... sanding and buffing and sanding some more.. <P><BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||MooCow||02-05-2001||08:50 AM||||Well I am done with all of the labor work just about.  I have already sanded everything and even primed some of the spots. Only thing I have left to do it put it back together and tape it all off to paint.  The wet sanding was actually fun.  I'm just worried that jch82 and I won't be able to put it back together.  Thanks for the info everyone.<P>                               Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-05-2001||02:16 PM||||put it back together to shoot it? your gunna jam all the parts first i hope, right. are you changing the color of the car? it's not hard to put the car back together... you've got 1000+ people here to direct you when you do somthing wrong..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  all my parts were shot off the car. we had to just hope and pray that the pearl matched up ok.. (it does.. but the nose is a bit light)||||reg||1
Z||000009||MooCow||02-05-2001||02:55 PM||||I was told that it isn't good to spray the body panels while off of the car.  I was told you must remove all body panels for a color change and spray the edges, then put back together, and then finally spray it and clear coat it.  What I need to know is how much clear coat to put on?  How many layers?  I want this paint job to last a while and don't want to have to do it again for some time so I am taking my time to do it right the first time.  I'm also still debating on the roof being black.<P>                                 Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FST2M6||02-05-2001||04:53 PM||||you can re assemble the car but you need to re-dis-assemble it to shoot the jams with clear or they will be the first area to start to flake and peel. you can shoot as may coats of clear as you wish. as long as the doors still open. <P>lay on a coat, let it flash lay on another coat. i've got 5 coats of clear. but 4 of which had pearl in them. <P>1 coat of sealer (block sand and prep-sol)<BR>2 coats of selfetching primer (block and prep)<BR>3 coats of orange<BR>2 coats of blue pearl<BR>2 coats of Gold pearl<BR>1 additional coat of clear no pearl. <P>the roof is just blocked, prep-sol, primed, blocked, prep-sol and shot.. it only has 2 coats of black and 2 coats clear. <P>the wing had the same as the roof but a bug died in the clear so we had to re-do the wing it's got 2 coats on the bottom and like 6 on top now.. but it's a mirror smooth finish. <P>once it was all done and re assembled the entire car was DA'd with 2000grit NO water and buffed with 3M buffing compound and waxed with 3M Show Car Glaze. i reglaze it once a month. and i've yet to have any water spots or anything.. the salt from the crappy michigan roads even rinsed off with just the hose... no elbow grease except for my wheels.<BR>||||reg||1
